  "uv_formula": {
    "x": "UVx_next = float32(Sign(UVx_current) * float32(float32(fmod(float64(abs(UVx_current)), 1.0)) + float32(color)))",
    "y": "UVy_next = float32(Sign(UVy_current) * float32(float32(fmod(float64(abs(UVy_current)), 1.0)) + float32(variant)))",
    "divisor_x": 1.0,
    "divisor_y": 1.0,
    "offsets": "color=0..14; variant=0..3; first transformed pair is color0/variant1, then 0/2,0/3,1/0,...,14/3. The list is mutated in place and each next pair reads the previous rewritten UV.",
    "ordinary_closed_form": "For fractions that survive float32 addition unchanged and signs that do not encounter zero: UVx=Sign(originalX)*(frac(abs(originalX))+color), UVy=Sign(originalY)*(frac(abs(originalY))+variant). Use the recurrence for exact reconstruction.",
    "signed_zero_exception": "Negative integer originalX produces -0 at color0/variant1; Mathf.Sign(-0)=+1 changes the next X to +0, and later color offsets become positive. Negative integer Y reaches -0 at color1/variant0; later variants become positive. Float32 offset addition can also round small/near-one fractions to integers; the next in-place modulo then uses that rounded value."
  },
